# XSH pthread_attr_getguardsize(), pthread_attr_setguardsize()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The default size and which sizes are invalid are not specified; the
# overflow protection itself cannot be observed portably.

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getguardsize.001
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getguardsize.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getguardsize.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       pthread_attr_setguardsize() with 0 (no guard area) returns 0,
           and pthread_attr_getguardsize() then returns 0 and stores 0.
test       t/001-zero.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getguardsize.002
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getguardsize.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       When pthread_attr_setguardsize() accepts the page size (and
           the page size plus 1), pthread_attr_getguardsize() stores
           exactly the value that was set, whether or not the
           implementation rounds the guard area up.
note       Whether a size is acceptable is not specified; a call that
           fails with EINVAL leaves the case unchecked, and the test is
           UNRESOLVED if the page size itself is refused.
test       t/002-round-trip.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getguardsize.003
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getguardsize.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       A thread created with a guard size of 0, and one with a guard
           size of one page, is created (0), runs its routine and can be
           joined, handing back the routine's return value.
note       pthread_create() failing with EAGAIN is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/003-create.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getguardsize.004
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getguardsize.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       pthread_attr_getguardsize() on a newly initialized attributes
           object returns 0.
note       The default value is implementation-defined and is not
           compared.
test       t/004-default.c
